    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`), including the new `AcceptanceTest` that asserts a fresh owner is capped at level 3.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement \u2014 membership level 4 requires tenure of more than 365 days, so a new (zero-tenure) owner never exceeds level 3 \u2014 was implemented entirely within a single file, `MembershipLevel.java`.\n\nKey design choice for low structural impact: `MembershipLevel.of(owner, namesakeCount)` already receives the `Owner`, which carries `registrationDate`. So the tenure factor is derived internally with **no signature change and no changes to the two callers** (`RespondWithOwner`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated`). That keeps the change to **one file, one edited method plus one small cohesive helper**:\n\n- `of` keeps its existing base logic (email + namesake, capped at 3) and only gains a single guarded promotion: `if (level == 3 && hasTenure(owner)) level = 4;` \u2014 so level 4 strictly requires both maxed base factors *and* tenure.\n- A new private `hasTenure(owner)` isolates the date arithmetic (`ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, now) > 365`), null-safe on `registrationDate`.\n\nA newly created owner's `registrationDate` is set to today by `BuildOwner`, giving zero tenure \u2192 the 3-member-household / email / namesake-0 owner lands at level 3, exactly as specified.",
